cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "drvec: exact maximum likelihood estimation of partially nonstationary VARMA models in VEC form"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the method paper it implements."
type: software
# The names and their order are the copyright line the sources carry
# (src/drvec.c:22 and README.md), not a fresh attribution.
authors:
  - family-names: "Mauricio"
    given-names: "J. A."
  - family-names: "Treadway"
    given-names: "A. B."
  - family-names: "Guerrero"
    given-names: "D. E."
version: "0.9"
date-released: "2026-08-22"
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/davidesg/drvec"
abstract: >-
  drvec estimates partially nonstationary vector ARMA models written in vector
  error-correction (VEC) form by exact maximum likelihood, using the
  transformation of Mauricio (2006): the VEC system is mapped onto a stationary
  VARMA model on the transformed vector, whose exact likelihood is evaluated by
  Algorithm AS 311.  It reports the cointegrating matrix and the adjustment
  matrix with standard errors, Wald tests of weak exogeneity and of exclusion
  from the long-run relations, a sequential likelihood-ratio test of the
  cointegration rank with an optional parametric bootstrap, multivariate
  residual diagnostics, and forecasts in levels with rolling-origin
  out-of-sample evaluation.  It shares its likelihood engine with drvarma and
  its parameter-file bridge with fue and drtran.
keywords:
  - cointegration
  - vector error correction
  - VARMA
  - exact maximum likelihood
  - time series
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Exact maximum likelihood estimation of partially nonstationary vector ARMA models"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Mauricio"
        given-names: "José Alberto"
    journal: "Computational Statistics & Data Analysis"
    volume: 50
    start: 3644
    end: 3662
    year: 2006
    doi: "10.1016/j.csda.2005.07.005"
